      "funding_type": "loan",
      "typical_award_size": "Special fund established 2003; initial capitalization fully expended, now replenished by loan repayments, interest and administration fees. Recent uses: $626,294 toward Bella Vista Inn interim housing rehabilitation (October 2026); Administration plans to request up to $2,500,000 for preservation of First Community Housing properties that carry $48,128,560 in County loans (six developments, 548 units).",
      "per_unit_cap": "None published.",
      "affordability_requirement": "Follows the recorded County regulatory agreement on the assisted property; preservation uses retain existing covenants.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "acquisition-rehab",
        "preservation"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "None. Case-by-case Board actions as loan modifications are presented (FCH portfolio report November 3, 2026).",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "santaclaracounty.gov subdomains (osh, asr, bhsd, news, files) returned HTTP 403 to automated access on 2026-11-07; records were built from the Board of Supervisors IQM2 legislative files (sccgov.iqm2.com), the County Housing Element, Santa Clara County Housing Authority documents, HCD and BOE pages. Small and opportunistic. The AHF matters mostly for sponsors acquiring distressed County-financed assets (FCH announced it will transfer all or part of its portfolio) and for sponsors needing County consent to subordinate, restructure or extend an existing County loan. OSH coordinates workouts with SCCHA and other lenders. Also the vehicle through which program income from closed sources (HOME repayments, Homekey and NPLH interest) is recycled.",
      "source_url": "https://sccgov.iqm2.com/Citizens/Detail_LegiFile.aspx?ID=130132",
